1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,792
My grandfather lied when he said time is an endless river. It is a finite, leaking tank.

2
00:00:07,092 --> 00:00:14,196
Every morning at dawn, I climb these wooden steps to wind the massive brass gears of our village clock.

3
00:00:14,496 --> 00:00:22,296
The town below depends on these hands moving. Without them, people freeze mid-step in the endless desert heat.

4
00:00:22,596 --> 00:00:29,604
Today, the main gear jammed. I forced my bare hands into the teeth, praying the metal wouldn't bite.

5
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:36,960
Blood smeared across the brass. But instead of stopping, the clock suddenly sped up with a sickening thud.

6
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:44,892
Then, I felt it. The rhythmic ticking inside the machine matched the exact frantic pace of my chest.

7
00:00:45,192 --> 00:00:52,152
I opened the master cylinder where the ancient pendulum should swing. There was no swinging weight inside.

8
00:00:52,452 --> 00:01:00,780
Instead, glowing cables snaked out of the wall, wrapping tightly around my wrists and feeding straight into my veins.

9
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:10,080
The townspeople down below finally moved again. They cheered, completely unaware whose life was fueling their morning.

10
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:15,924
Would you keep your heart beating if every tick erased someone you loved from existence?
